@@ -0,0 +1,62 @@
+# Root SDK controller (actual container, GPU gate)
+
+Author did not run Docker, GPU, CUDA, Torch, NVCC, network or a device compile.
+The primary controller is `root-v1/qwen35_vl_sdk_controller.py`; it stages the
+untouched `native/native_whole_model.py` b66 C-API implementation and actual
+image/video fixtures into the existing `infinity-torch214-compare-sdk` container.
+It does not compile a host tower and does not create a new container.
+
+## 0. Host pins (no Docker)
+
+```bash
+cd /tmp/oxide-all-model-feature-matrix-v1/qwen35-vl-full-v1
+CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' taskset -c 88-95 \
+  python3 root-v1/qwen35_vl_sdk_controller.py --pins
+```
+
+This freezes the controller/source/fixture files, original config/index metadata,
+the pinned consumer SHA, and the union124 manifest.
+
+## 1. Executable CPU stage inside the actual SDK container (before GPU quality)
+
+```bash
+cd /tmp/oxide-all-model-feature-matrix-v1/qwen35-vl-full-v1
+python3 root-v1/qwen35_vl_sdk_controller.py --phase cpu --run \
+  --output /tmp/oxide-qwen35vl-sdk-output/cpu-$(date +%s)
+```
+
+Requires Root and the existing container. It:
+- preserves `DOCKER_CONFIG`, registry credentials, proxy and CA variables; removes
+  only `DOCKER_HOST/CONTEXT/TLS*`;
+- strips inherited `CUDA_/INFINITY_/LD_` selectors;
+- stages under a fresh `/tmp/oxide-qwen35vl-sdk/<run-id>` path;
+- runs each command under the inner `remote_guard.py` with
+  `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=''`, `taskset -c 88-95`;
+- validates b66 SHA `b66d70b6…`, Torch `2.14.1+cu130`/git
+  `5c488690…`, vendor `libcublasLt` 13.2 GOT binding, union124 manifest
+  `56863d52270f04e2a72c07f0213295cb78cd003ec111239bef1f78e75ea720c5`
+  with 124/124/124 symbols, original config/index/header and actual
+  single-image/two-image/three-frame video fixture shapes;
+- runs `native_whole_model.py --plan-only` for every model/fixture.
+No engine, CUDA context, or weight payload is created in the CPU phase.
+
+## 2. GPU0 whole-model quality (Root only)
+
+```bash
+python3 root-v1/qwen35_vl_sdk_controller.py --phase quality --run \
+  --output /tmp/oxide-qwen35vl-sdk-output/quality-$(date +%s)
+```
+
+Runs the same staged b66 implementation with `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0`; Elephant
+and Mammoth use `--decision`. Paired Oxide whole-model capture is the next gate
+using `consumer whole-factory` and `pair-whole`; no parity claim is made here.
+
+## Runtime/profile policy
+
+- Union124 runtime: `/tmp/infinity-oxide-parity-20261101/device-union124-all3-v1/kernels`
+  (old99 bodies + PTX preserved for all three arches, new25 ABI all3).
+- Canonical26 FA4 is sufficient for dense Qwen3.5-VL (dynamic-head ratio ABI).
+- Mode26 is only the 35B-A3B ratio8 text tail; MoE text remains with its owner.
+- Pinned optimized host consumer:
+  `target-opt3-noLTO/release/qwen35-vl-consumer`
+  sha256 `e8bf05960d100b689ff3c50bb7ce2ed4565453d25972941ba3b71be0281a29e0`.
